    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1205">

                <pb facs="0983" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5448.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Durango to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Durango</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-09T10:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1912—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Northeastern portion of Durango in rebel possession, estimated 2,000; also as
                    many more in extreme eastern part of State of Durango; numerous other small
                    rebel and bandit bands nearly all sections.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamm.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
